A frontend-only project must not require a server runtime. A backend-only project must not download a browser UI runtime. A middleware-only project must not require a component compiler. A complete application should be able to use the full stack with minimal configuration.

## 0.3 Product principles

1. Small core, optional capabilities.
2. Native TypeScript support.
3. Standards-based web APIs wherever possible.
4. Minimal runtime overhead.
5. Predictable rendering and state updates.
